\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Probability pushforwards require a positive source}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The probability theorem \ref{fdip-00G8} starts with
an already reflection-positive source measure. Its map is
measurable and intertwines the configuration reflections,
and each target positive-half observable pulls back to a
source positive-half observable. On finite configuration
spaces, that pullback is the algebra map of
\ref{fdip-00XI}.}

\p{A Berezin coefficient is a signed linear functional,
so applying that probability theorem first requires an
actual probability measure with the stated positivity.
For an algebraic restriction, \ref{fdip-00XI} instead
requires multiplicativity and half-preservation.
A linear projector that combines both halves has neither
property merely because it is idempotent.}
